From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:01:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add overfitting diagnostic; fix findings of the
 review-fix verification

Overfitting diagnostic (src/evaluation/overfitting_diagnostic.py,
Team_Review/multimodal/overfitting/): the recorded fusion / image-only / text-only runs are
retrained byte-identically with every epoch scored on train and validation in eval() mode with
one loss definition, plus a head-size / regularization sweep (fusion vs image only, 3 seeds).
The heads memorize the training set; reducing that does not improve validation or let fusion
beat image only. Report, review README, experiment log and PoC notebook now separate observed,
tested and inferred statements.

Fixes: .gitignore inline comment that disabled /features/; batch serving keeps one decoded
image at a time; Pillow decompression-bomb cap returns 413; body limit allows wrapped base64;
format allow-list test that cannot pass vacuously; complete list of dataset-derived files in
Git; doc examples that collided with shipped run IDs; clearer evaluate/error_analysis errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012mxouBDiknGrGqchsM6QFE
